#!/usr/bin/env sh
# peaks-loop push gate. Design + why-it-is-a-ratchet: .husky/peaks-gate.mjs
#
# Legs 2 and 3 are scoped to WHAT YOU ARE PUSHING (slice B5, 2026-09-23). Leg 1
# is the ONE whole-tree measurement here — it does not look only at the diff —
# and it earns its place because it is a SET RATCHET, not a whole-repo boolean:
# it exits 0 while the unformatted set stays INSIDE a named baseline of 12
# pre-existing files, and names any file outside it. (`pnpm format:check` is the
# boolean form, red on arrival on this tree, and is deliberately NOT used.)
#
# ORDER IS CHEAPEST-FIRST AND REWRITES-FIRST, and the second half is the real
# reason. Leg 1 is ~12s measured on this host (2026-10-10); leg 2 is a type-aware
# eslint program; leg 3 is minutes. But leg 1's FIX is `pnpm format`, which
# REWRITES tracked source — and that invalidates the other two: leg 2 recomputes
# its per-file verdicts from content, and leg 3 classified a diff and ran suites
# against the old bytes. Run last, a formatting breach would force a full re-run
# of both expensive legs. Run first, every expensive leg runs on the tree that
# will actually be pushed, and the mechanical fix is out of the way before you
# read results you would otherwise have to throw away.
#
#   1. `node .husky/format-check-ratchet.mjs` — the EXACT command CI's
#      `format set ratchet` job runs (.github/workflows/ci.yml, job id
#      `format-check`). Until this leg existed NOTHING local ran it, and that is
#      not carelessness, it is structure: leg 2 is a per-file eslint ratchet and
#      never looks at formatting, and leg 3 runs tests, of which this is not one.
#      So CI was the first and only grader — and it went red twice on one night
#      (2026-10-10) on two files the SAME round had added,
#      container-docker-boundary.test.ts then capability-audit-gate-diagnostic.test.ts,
#      each time after a green push gate. A leg nothing runs is not a leg; this
#      one now fails here on exactly the input CI would fail on.
#
#   2. `changed` mode — the SAME per-file ratchet as the commit gate, applied to
#      `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` instead of the index. A file you
#      touched may not be worse than its own line in
#      .peaks/lint/gate-baseline.json; a file the diff ADDS must be clean; a file
#      the diff DELETES contributes 0 and is not handed to eslint.
#
#   3. `pnpm test:changed` — the repo's EXISTING affected-tests mechanism
#      (scripts/test-changed.mjs, wired since slice 2 as `test:changed`). Not a
#      new script: it classifies the same diff and runs the tests that diff
#      implies, falling back to the FULL unit suite for a change it declines to
#      reason about (package.json / pnpm-lock.yaml / vitest.config.ts /
#      tsconfig.json / scripts/ / .claude/ / .peaks/, or an empty diff).
#
#      THE RULES LIVE IN ONE MODULE: scripts/test-changed-classify.mjs (pure; pinned
#      by tests/unit/scripts/test-changed-classify.test.ts and the wiring arm in
#      tests/unit/scripts/test-changed-git-env.test.ts). Three of them are not obvious,
#      and each exists because this hook was measured letting a defect through
#      (rid 2026-10-10-gate-classifier-backstop-repair):
#        - `.peaks/lint/gate-baseline.json` is NOT a 0-test exemption any more. Its
#          reader is `BASELINE_PATH` in tests/unit/standards/_file-size-cap-scan.ts,
#          which the 2026-09-23 "no test reads it" search could not see (it looked
#          for the path string, and the reader reaches the file through a constant).
#          A diff that MOVES the artifact's content runs the suites that guard it —
#          tests/unit/standards/ and tests/unit/lint/. A regeneration that moves only
#          `generatedAt` is inert: 0 tests, and the run says so out loud.
#        - any A/D/R/C in the diff — the file SET changed, not just one file's
#          contents — runs tests/unit/standards/: the whole-tree population guards
#          (baseline `files[]` completeness among them), which no `src/<area>`
#          mapping reaches. That is the arm that catches "added a gated file and
#          never regenerated the baseline".
#        - src/services/scan/file-size-policy.ts DEFINES that population, so an M-only
#          edit to it (adding one extension brings dozens of tracked files into scope)
#          runs the same guards.
#
#      The guards are an ADDITION to a mapping, never a substitute for the fallback:
#      a diff that reaches no mapping at all (README.md, .github/**, .husky/**, docs/**,
#      a deleted test file) runs the FULL suite. While the guards fed the mapping those
#      diffs selected 13 guard files and the fallback never fired — a false green of the
#      same class as the defect above.
#
#      What it is today, measured on this host 2026-10-10 (the baseline rows re-measured
#      for the repair; the others from the same round's slice):
#        - baseline `generatedAt`-only regeneration -> 0 tests,             exit 0
#        - a diff MOVING the baseline's content     -> 47 files / 445 tests, 110s
#          (tests/unit/standards + tests/unit/lint; both suites guard the artifact)
#        - a diff reaching no mapping at all        -> the FULL suite, see below
#        - a content-only `src/cli/commands/**` diff -> 71 files / 601 tests,  61s
#        - an ADDED file under `src/cli/commands/`   -> 84 files / 765 tests,  75s
#          (the area subset PLUS the whole-tree guards)
#        - a diff that also touches package.json / scripts/ / .peaks/
#                                                    ->427 files /4486 tests, 320s
#      So the hook is 0 tests, a subset, or the full suite depending on the diff, and the
#      old "936s, a known measured gap" no longer describes it. Do not skip it with
#      --no-verify on the strength of a stale number.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT A WEAKER GATE THAN THE WHOLE-REPO ONE IT REPLACED
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The baseline stores a number PER FILE, so the per-file check is not a proxy
# for the total check — it is the total check, decomposed:
#
#     every changed file ≤ its own baseline        (leg 2, per file)
#     AND every new file contributes 0             (leg 2, per file)
#     AND every deleted file contributes 0         (leg 2 drops it entirely)
#   ⟹ total = Σ(untouched files' baselines) + Σ(changed files' actuals) + 0
#            ≤ Σ(all baselines) ≤ the whole-repo ceiling.
#
# Measured against the 2026-09-22 baseline: Σ(per-file eslint baselines) = 2878,
# exactly the `eslintFindings` ceiling — an identity here, not an approximation.
# So if this file passes, the whole-repo totals it used to check CANNOT have
# grown upward. That is an entailment; the old check was the special case of it.
#
# What the per-file check cannot see: growth on a file NOBODY touched, caused by
# CONFIG DRIFT (a rule quietly switched off or on, a phantom rule appearing, a
# coverage hole opening). That class is rare, real, and is nobody's commit — so
# it is paid for by a machine instead of by a human waiting to push. CI owns it:
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `vitest + build` job, step "Whole-repo lint
# ratchet", runs `node .husky/peaks-gate.mjs repo`. That job already ran the full
# unit suite (`npx vitest run`), so the ratchet was the only missing piece — the
# two coexist and do not overlap (the ratchet contains no tests).
#
# WHY IT MOVED AT ALL: `repo` mode is ~9 type-aware eslint programs (each
# rebuilding the TS program) plus a whole-program `tsc`, and its cost is a
# function of the WHOLE REPO. The changed mode's cost is a function of the DIFF:
# measured on this host 2026-09-23, the whole-repo gate took 126s, the same gate
# over a 49-file slice took 7s. (The slice that requested this change recorded
# 8+ minutes for the repo gate; that number did NOT reproduce here — 126s on
# re-measurement — and this repo has been burned before by a number taken while
# other work ran on the same box. Neither figure is the point: the point is that
# the pre-push cost no longer grows with the size of the repository.) A push gate
# that costs minutes stops being a "check it before I push" and becomes a thing
# people skip with `--no-verify` — and a gate people skip is worse than no gate,
# because it is also believed.
set -e
node .husky/format-check-ratchet.mjs
node .husky/peaks-gate.mjs changed
pnpm test:changed -- origin/main
